[{"id":"29821","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>When the Chauhans tried to expand towards the west and east, from whom did they face opposition?</span></p>","option_1":"Gahadavalas and Turks","option_2":"Chalukyas of Gujarat and Gahadavalas","option_3":"Rajputs and Tughlaqs","option_4":"Khiljis and Chalukyas","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Chalukyas of Gujarat and Gahadavalas.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The Chahamanas (Chauhans) of Ajmer, under rulers like Prithviraj III, faced opposition from the Chalukyas (Solankis) of Gujarat while expanding westward and from the Gahadavalas of Kannauj while expanding eastward, making these two powers their principal rivals in that period.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29822","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Prasanta Chandra Mahalanobis established the ______.</span></p>","option_1":"Reserve Bank of India","option_2":"State Bank of India","option_3":"Indian Statistical Institute","option_4":"National Sample Survey Office","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Indian Statistical Institute.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>P.C. Mahalanobis, a renowned Indian statistician, founded the Indian Statistical Institute (ISI) in Kolkata in 1931. He is also known for the Mahalanobis distance and his contribution to India's Second Five-Year Plan strategy.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29823","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which one of the following chronological order (from first to last) regarding the rule of early Turkish rulers is correct?</span></p>","option_1":"Qutbuddin Aybak, Shamsuddin Iltutmish, Ghiyasuddin Balban","option_2":"Ghiyasuddin Balban, Qutbuddin Aybak, Shamsuddin Iltutmish","option_3":"Shamsuddin Iltutmish, Ghiyasuddin Balban, Qutbuddin Aybak","option_4":"Ghiyasuddin Balban, Shamsuddin Iltutmish, Qutbuddin Aybak","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Qutbuddin Aybak, Shamsuddin Iltutmish, Ghiyasuddin Balban.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Qutbuddin Aybak founded the Delhi Sultanate (Slave/Mamluk dynasty) in 1206, followed by Shamsuddin Iltutmish (1211-1236), who consolidated the Sultanate, and later Ghiyasuddin Balban (1266-1287), who strengthened royal authority. This is the correct chronological order.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29824","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following five year plans had the theme \"Towards Faster and More Inclusive Growth\"?</span></p>","option_1":"First","option_2":"Fifth","option_3":"Seventh","option_4":"Eleventh","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"",