d":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29828","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following articles of the Indian Constitution deals with the power of Parliament to legislate with respect to any matter in the State List if a Proclamation of Emergency is in operation?</span></p>","option_1":"Article 282","option_2":"Article 250","option_3":"Article 263","option_4":"Article 173","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Article 250.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Article 250 of the Indian Constitution empowers Parliament to make laws on any matter in the State List while a Proclamation of Emergency (under Article 352) is in operation, temporarily converting India's federal structure into a unitary one.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29829","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>'Gaarudi Gombe', performed during major festivals, is a folk dance of which Indian state/Union Territory?</span></p>","option_1":"West Bengal","option_2":"Karnataka","option_3":"Tripura","option_4":"Jammu and Kashmir","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Karnataka.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Gaarudi Gombe (also spelt Garudi Gombe) is a traditional folk dance from Karnataka, performed by dancers wearing large bamboo-and-cloth puppet frames resembling mythological figures, typically during temple festivals and celebrations like Dasara.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29830","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Meristematic tissue is classified into how many types?</span></p>","option_1":"2","option_2":"3","option_3":"4","option_4":"5","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - 3.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Meristematic tissue in plants is classified into three types based on location: apical meristem (at root and shoot tips), lateral meristem (e.g., vascular and cork cambium), and intercalary meristem (found at the base of leaves/internodes).</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29831","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>In which Indian state/UT is the 'Three Kings Feast' festival celebrated?</span></p>","option_1":"Goa","option_2":"Ladakh","option_3":"Nagaland","option_4":"Assam","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Goa.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The 'Feast of the Three Kings' (Feast of Reis Magos) is celebrated in Goa on 6 January every year at Cansaulim, Chandor, and Reis Magos villages, commemorating the biblical visit of the Three Wise Men to baby Jesus, reflecting Goa's Portuguese Christian heritage.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29832","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>According to Census 2011, which state had the highest sex ratio in India?</span></p>","option_1":"Tamil Nadu","option_2":"Kerala","option_3":"Puducherry","option_4":"Goa","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Kerala.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>As per Census 2011, Kerala recorded the highest sex ratio among Indian states, with 1,084 females per 1,000 males, attributed to better healthcare, literacy, and social indicators for women in the state.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29833","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"778","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The recoil experienced when firing a bullet from a gun is an example of ______.</span></p>","option_1":"Newton's second law of motion","option_2":"Newton's law of gravitation","option_3":"Newton's third law of motion","option_4":"Newton's first law of motion","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Newton's third law of motion.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Newton's Third Law states that for every action there is an equal and opposite reaction. When a bullet is fired forward (action), the gun recoils backward with an equal and opposite force (reaction) — this is the principle behind gun recoil.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"